  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Adaptation Water and Energy Infrastructure Programme (CAWEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through UNICEF, the FCDO funded programme is supporting the development of climate resilient, multiple use water and renewable energy infrastructure in vulnerable communities of Zimbabwe. .	 UNICEF manages this component  that provides sustainable basic water supply  using climate resilient infrastructure, through the installation of solar powered water schemes in 9 districts. UNICEF holds implementing partnerships with  are Welthungerhilfe, CAFOD, Mercy Corps and Christian Care. Ministry of Lands, Agriculture, Fisheries, Water and Rural Resettlement, Department of Climate Change Management (CCMD) and the District Development Fund (DDF).</narrative>
  </description>
